From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: N0zoM1z0 <161784452+N0zoM1z0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:05:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [th02/main] Decompile main() and the stage-independent
 initialization

The three C++ units after main() now share ZUN's single main_01_TEXT
segment. TLINK then emits the original `NOP; PUSH CS; CALL near` for far
calls within that segment by itself, as seen for demo_load(), GameExecl()
and DemoPlay(). Calls to segments that ReC98 still keeps separate retain
the inline-asm stand-in.
---
 th02/main_01a.cpp | 119 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 th02/main_01b.cpp |   4 +-
 th02/main_01c.cpp |   2 +-
 th02_main.asm     | 256 +++++-----------------------------------------
 4 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 236 deletions(-)

